  {
   "id": 667829,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stem_html": "<p>Cash kicked a football off a tee. The path of the football is shown below and represented by the function <span data-math=\"f(x)=-0 .02(x-h)^2+k\">f(x)=-0 .02(x-h)^2+k</span>, where <span data-math=\"x\">x</span> represents the horizontal distance and <span data-math=\"f(x)\">f(x)</span> represents the height.</p>\n<p><img height=\"265\" src=\"exercises/media/b228a105dde60677.jpg\" width=\"300\" alt=\"Graph displays a parabolic path, charting height in feet against horizontal distance in feet. The orange curve shows an object's trajectory, starting above zero, peaking at ~6 ft, and landing at ~30 ft.\"></p>\n<p>Find the vertex and its meaning.</p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1332249,
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"(30, 0)\">(30, 0)</span>, the football travels 30 feet before hitting the ground."
    },
    {
     "id": 1332250,
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"(14,5)\">(14,5)</span> the football hit its highest height of 14 feet after traveling 5 feet."
    },
    {
     "id": 1332251,
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"(14,5)\">(14,5)</span>, the football hit its highest height of 5 feet after traveling 14 feet."
    },
    {
     "id": 1332252,
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"(0,1)\">(0,1)</span>, the ball was kicked from a height of 1 foot."
    }
   ],
